"\\\"vitest run tests/unit\\\",\\\"typecheck\\\":\\\"tsc --noEmit\\\",\\\"test:public\\\":\\\"node --test scripts/*.test.mjs\\\",\\\"build:public\\\":\\\"node scripts/build-public.mjs\\\",\\\"verify:public\\\":\\\"node scripts/verify-public.mjs\\\"},\\\"_npmUser\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"},\\\"_resolved\\\":\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-svidyuk-me-flop-core--claude-worktrees-issue-grooming-triage-cd2a2a/e6f8f9ef-a4b2-4f41-95d7-9737f3556783/scratchpad/npm-bootstrap/tarballs/flop-labs-cli-0.4.0.tgz\\\",\\\"_integrity\\\":\\\"sha512-X38hpJKsF/GqLMcLKhiG4QldCSRudEr6Lci5wUK9QyBQ7BuKYNVpBmBdKoQS6R/f9qK8wN9p/ALuAIq5xrSqqg==\\\",\\\"repository\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"git+https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core.git\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"git\\\",\\\"directory\\\":\\\"sdk/cli\\\"},\\\"_npmVersion\\\":\\\"11.15.0\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"FLOP Network CLI \u2014 interact with FLOP from the terminal\\\",\\\"directories\\\":{},\\\"_nodeVersion\\\":\\\"24.16.0\\\",\\\"dependencies\\\":{\\\"commander\\\":\\\"^15.0.0\\\",\\\"@polkadot/api\\\":\\\"^17.0.1\\\",\\\"@flop-labs/sdk\\\":\\\"^0.4.0\\\",\\\"@flop-labs/client\\\":\\\"^0.2.1\\\",\\\"@polkadot/keyring\\\":\\\"^14.0.3\\\",\\\"@polkadot/util-crypto\\\":\\\"^14.0.3\\\"},\\\"publishConfig\\\":{\\\"access\\\":\\\"public\\\"},\\\"_hasShrinkwrap\\\":false,\\\"devDependencies\\\":{\\\"tsx\\\":\\\"^4.23.15\\\",\\\"vitest\\\":\\\"^4.1.12\\\",\\\"esbuild\\\":\\\"0.28.2\\\",\\\"typescript\\\":\\\"^7.0.2\\\",\\\"@types/node\\\":\\\"^26.6.2\\\",\\\"@polkadot/types\\\":\\\"^17.0.1\\\",\\\"@flop-labs/agent-sdk\\\":\\\"0.2.0\\\",\\\"@flop-labs/gateway-core\\\":\\\"0.2.0\\\"},\\\"_npmOperationalInternal\\\":{\\\"tmp\\\":\\\"tmp/cli_0.4.0_1793246535562_0.2994485607096383\\\",\\\"host\\\":\\\"s3://npm-registry-packages-npm-production\\\"}}},\\\"time\\\":{\\\"created\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T04:00:59.319Z\\\",\\\"modified\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:13:06.599Z\\\",\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T04:00:59.319Z\\\",\\\"0.4.0\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T04:02:15.653Z\\\"},\\\"bugs\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core/issues\\\"},\\\"license\\\":\\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\",\\\"homepage\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core#readme\\\",\\\"repository\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"git+https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core.git\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"git\\\",\\\"directory\\\":\\\"sdk/cli\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"FLOP Network CLI \u2014 interact with FLOP from the terminal\\\",\\\"maintainers\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"}],\\\"readme\\\":\\\"# @flop-labs/cli\\\\n\\\\nFLOP Network CLI \u2014 interact with FLOP Network nodes from the command line.\\\\n\\\\n## Installation\\\\n\\\\nThe full CLI (key, miner, validator and model commands) needs Node.js 22+. Run a pinned release\\\\nfrom public npm without installing it globally:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nnpx --yes --package @flop-labs/cli@0.4.0 flop --version\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nOr run the promoted container image, which needs only Docker. For a reproducible digest pin,\\\\nuse [releases.json](https://flop.network/releases.json). The image starts in `/app`, so mount\\\\nyour working directory and pass absolute paths under it:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\ndocker run --rm --network host -v \\\\\\\"$PWD:/work\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\n  ghcr.io/flop-labs/flop-core/cli:stable \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --version\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`npm install --global @flop-labs/cli` also works, but it puts a second `flop` on `PATH`: the\\\\npublic Hermes launcher's installer below refuses to install next to it, and the two commands\\\\nshadow each other.\\\\n\\\\nFor the recommended public native Hermes provider path, install the standalone launcher without repository\\\\nor package-registry access:\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\ncurl -fsSL https://flop.network/releases/cli/0.4.11/install.sh | sh -s -- --version 0.4.11\\\\nexport PATH=\\\\\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\\\\\\\"\\\\nflop --network devnet hermes desktop --doctor\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThis release needs Node.js 22+, curl and the qualified Hermes 0.22.2 release. It contains the hosted\\\\nHermes commands and the native public provider 0.1.6 and preserves an existing full CLI. See the\\\\npublic launcher guide (`docs/integrations/hermes-public-launcher.md` in the FLOP repository) for\\\\nthe native setup sequence, checksums, the 24-hour trial and acceptance limits.\\\\nThe alternate hosted launcher needs explicit preparation of its generated Hermes\\\\nhome; it is not qualified as a one-step launch on a fresh managed installation. The full CLI\\\\nsource build remains:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\\\\npnpm --filter @flop-labs/gateway-core build\\\\npnpm --filter @flop-labs/sdk exec tsc\\\\npnpm --filter @flop-labs/sdk run build:a2a-cjs\\\\npnpm --filter @flop-labs/agent-sdk exec tsc\\\\npnpm --filter @flop-labs/cli build\\\\nnode sdk/cli/dist/cli.js --version # from the repository root\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop [options] [command]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Global Options\\\\n\\\\n| Option | Description | Default |\\\\n|--------|-------------|---------|\\\\n| `--network <name>` | `local`, `devnet`, `testnet`, or `mainnet` | `local` |\\\\n| `--rpc <url>` | Explicit RPC override | selected profile |\\\\n| `--signer <uri>` | Local signer URI | `//Alice` on local only |\\\\n| `--keystore <path>` | Encrypted Polkadot JSON keystore | \u2014 |\\\\n| `--password-env <name>` | Environment variable containing its password | \u2014 |\\\\n| `--output <mode>` | `human`, pretty `json`, or compact `agent` | `human` |\\\\n| `--json` | Output as JSON | false |\\\\n\\\\n### Commands\\\\n\\\\n#### Unified role onboarding\\\\n\\\\nThe role commands provide one entry point for onboarding, diagnostics, status,\\\\nand lifecycle operations. `init` and `doctor` are read-only. Commands such as\\\\n`register`, `calibrate-start`, `commission`, `unjail`, `rejoin`, and `exit`\\\\nare explicit chain mutations.\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\n# Agents: the devnet tailnet MCP is read-only; local mode is signer-capable.\\\\nflop --network devnet agent init --client codex\\\\nflop --network devnet agent doctor\\\\nflop agent launch codex\\\\nflop agent proxy\\\\nflop agent hermes desktop\\\\nflop keys generate --out agent-key.json --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD\\\\nflop agent wallet create <agent-address>\\\\nflop agent session create --delegate <address>\\\\n\\\\n# Miners: sim first, measured TDX for verified production, cloud is non-attested.\\\\nflop miner init --mode sim\\\\nflop miner doctor --mode sim\\\\nflop miner status [address]\\\\nflop --signer <MINER-URI> miner register --commission 10\\\\nflop --signer <MINER-URI> miner calibrate-start\\\\n\\\\n# Validators: live stake minimum and PoUI-gated committee state are queried.\\\\nflop validator init --mode local\\\\nflop validator doctor\\\\nflop validator status [address]\\\\nflop --signer <VALIDATOR-URI> validator register\\\\nflop --signer <VALIDATOR-URI> validator commission 10\\\\nflop --signer <VALIDATOR-URI> validator unjail\\\\nflop --signer <VALIDATOR-URI> validator rejoin\\\\nflop --signer <VALIDATOR-URI> validator exit\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nAll role planning and diagnostic commands support `--json` for automation.\\\\nGlobal network and custody options work at any nesting depth.\\\\n\\\\n#### Networks and faucet\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop --network devnet network status\\\\nflop --network devnet faucet request <address>\\\\nflop --network testnet faucet request <address> --amount 25\\\\nflop --network mainnet network status       # planned; no faucet\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFaucet requests compare the RPC and faucet `/chain` genesis hashes before\\\\nrequesting funds. A recognized RPC conflicting with explicit `--network` is\\\\nrejected.\\\\n\\\\n#### Agent-efficient output\\\\n\\\\nUse `--output agent` for a stable, single-line JSON result with no banners,\\\\nemoji, indentation, or successful `doctor` checks:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop --output agent miner doctor --mode tdx\\\\nflop --output agent validator status <address>\\\\nflop --output agent agent init --client codex\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSuccesses include `ok:true`. Failures go to stderr with a nonzero exit and a\\\\ncompact `code`, `message`, `retryable`, and optional `next` action. `--json`\\\\nremains the backward-compatible pretty JSON format. Interactive processes such\\\\nas `launch`, `proxy`, and Hermes itself retain their application output after\\\\nstartup; use Hermes `--dry-run` for a one-shot agent-readable launch plan.\\\\n\\\\n#### Health\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop health           # Human-readable\\\\nflop health --json    # JSON output\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### Balance\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop balance 5Grwva8T1BQxqNJJM...       # Check account balance\\\\nflop balance 5Grwva8... --json             # JSON output\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### GPU Detection\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop gpu              # Detect local GPUs\\\\nflop gpu --json       # JSON output\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### Declared GPU inventory\\\\n```bash\\\\nnvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,memory.total --format=csv,noheader,nounits > gpus.csv\\\\nflop --keystore miner.json --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD miner declare-gpu --nvidia-smi gpus.csv\\\\nflop miner declare-gpu --detect --dry-run   # on the GPU host itself; prints the remark only\\\\nflop --keystore miner.json --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD miner declare-gpu --retract   # withdraw it\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nA registered miner publishes the GPUs it runs as a signed `flop.gpu-inventory.v1` remark (format:\\\\n`docs/design/gpu-inventory-remark.md` in the FLOP repository), so explorers can show its hardware. It is\\\\nself-reported and display-only: calibration caps, SKU ceilings and rewards never read it. The CLI\\\\nimage cannot run the host's `nvidia-smi`, so pass its output with `--nvidia-smi` (`-` reads stdin).\\\\n\\\\n#### Stake Info\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop info 5Grwva8...  # Get miner stake info\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### Session Keys\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop session create --delegate <address> --daily-cap 50 --tx-limit 5\\\\nflop session list --owner <address>\\\\nflop --signer <DELEGATE-URI> chat --session-owner <OWNER> \\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\"\\\\nflop --signer <DELEGATE-URI> proxy --session-owner <OWNER>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSession inference checks activity, expiry, and per-tx/daily/lifetime budgets,\\\\nthen submits the HTLC through `executeViaSession`. `chat` persists conversation\\\\nIDs and supports `--conversation`, `--history`, and `--delete`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Named-miner inference\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop --network devnet --keystore agent.json --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD \\\\\\\\\\\\n  session run --miner MINER_SS58 --model qwen/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --endpoint MINER_HTTPS_URL --prompt 'Reply OK.' --max-flop 0.01 --max-tokens 8 --json\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe completion limit defaults to 256 tokens. `--max-tokens` must be a positive safe\\\\ninteger; `--max-flop` bounds escrow separately. JSON includes `finish_reason` and\\\\n`completion_tokens`; `length` means the response reached its token limit. The turn\\\\ndeadline remains 60 seconds, so large token limits or slow inference can still time\\\\nout and follow normal channel recovery. Settlement separately waits for the miner's\\\\non-chain calibrated allowance; faster inference does not bypass that limit. Legacy miners may require\\\\n`--auth-token-env MINER_SESSION_BEARER`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Models\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop model list\\\\nflop model get <hash-or-name> --precision FP16\\\\nflop model fetch <hash-or-name> --output-dir ./weights\\\\nflop model fetch <hash> --source hf:org/repo --precision INT8\\\\nflop --signer <PUBLISHER> model upload --model-hash <hash> --path ./weights\\\\nBASE=http://miner:8000 DECODE_POLICY_HASH=0x<hash> \\\\\\\\\\\\n  flop --network local model onboard --source org/model --precision BF16\\\\n\\\\n# Existing-commitment recovery/advanced mode:\\\\nflop --signer <PUBLISHER> model upload \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --model-hash <hash> --commitment <0x-hash> --size <bytes>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFetch accepts `hf:`, `modelscope:`, HTTPS, and `da:` sources and writes only\\\\nafter dm-verity matches the registered root. Full upload builds the canonical\\\\nimage, runs `da-validator submit`, registers its leased blob, and binds it.\\\\nOnboard additionally registers the model, mirrors, per-precision measured root,\\\\nand decode policy, but only after the serving endpoint passes capture replay,\\\\nbinding rejection, and output-coherence probes. Re-running it submits no writes.\\\\n`--hf-repo owner/model` gives a local `--source` a Hugging Face mirror, but only\\\\nafter that repo reproduces the measured root. Re-running with it adds the mirror\\\\nto an already registered model.\\\\n\\\\n#### Gateway configuration\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nexport MINER_GATEWAY_TOKEN='from-a-secret-manager'\\\\nflop gateway allowlist \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --miner https://miner.example \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --network devnet \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --auth-token-env MINER_GATEWAY_TOKEN \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --attestation ./gateway-attestation.json \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --json\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe command emits ready-to-use `GATEWAY_SESSION_ALLOWLIST` and\\\\n`GATEWAY_MODEL_CATALOG` string values. The selected network supplies the RPC\\\\ndefault. It anonymously probes `/session/info` first to require bearer auth,\\\\nthen checks every advertised identity field against `model-registry`, including\\\\nthe measured root and decode-policy allowlist, and checks the miner's calibration\\\\nagainst the finalized `hw-calibration` snapshot.\\\\n\\\\nThe attestation file uses `schema_version: \\\\\\\"flop.gateway-attestation.v1\\\\\\\"` and\\\\ncontains `broker` limits, `deployment` evidence, and `catalog` evidence. The\\\\ncatalog block is a `CanonicalModelRecord` without the generated identity fields\\\\nor `prices`; it carries one `price` snapshot instead. Deployment\\\\n`observedAt`/`expiresAt`, catalog price validity, and feature conformance are\\\\nused unchanged. Expired evidence is refused rather than refreshed.\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\n# GATEWAY_SESSION_ALLOWLIST / GATEWAY_MODEL_CATALOG hold the gateway's own values.\\\\nexport GPUAI_API_KEY='from-a-secret-manager'\\\\nexport GATEWAY_RENEWER_SIGNER_URI='dedicated funded account, not the broker signer'\\\\nflop --network devnet gateway renew \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --allowlist-env GATEWAY_SESSION_ALLOWLIST \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --catalog-env GATEWAY_MODEL_CATALOG --catalog-pricing chain \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --provider-key-env GPUAI_API_KEY \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --probe-signer-env GATEWAY_RENEWER_SIGNER_URI --probe-escrow 1 \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --out /opt/flop/gateway-evidence/gateway-evidence.json\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`gateway renew` re-makes that evidence instead of re-stamping it, and writes\\\\nthe file the gateway hot-reloads as `GATEWAY_EVIDENCE_FILE`. A miner's\\\\ndeployment is renewed only when GPU.ai still reports the instance named in\\\\n`deployment.source` (`operator-observed:gpu.ai/<instance> <region> <gpu>`,\\\\noptionally followed by a `(label)`) as `running` in that region on that GPU. The\\\\nGPU is GPU.ai's identifier (`rtx_a6000`) or its name in GPU.ai's GPU type table\\\\n(`RTX A6000`, with or without `NVIDIA`); any other name is not renewed. A\\\\ntailnet-hosted miner (`operator-observed:tailscale/<host> egress <ipv4> AS<n>`,\\\\noptionally followed by the network's name and a `(label)`) is renewed only while the\\\\nhost's tailscaled (`--tailscale-socket`) sees exactly one node of that name online,\\\\ntagged `tag:miner`, on a direct path from that egress address; the country stamped\\\\nfrom that address therefore still holds. Its authenticated `/session/info` must also still advertise the pinned address,\\\\nenclave key, and identity that the\\\\nfinalized chain still admits. A record's `tools` conformance is renewed only by\\\\na real compute-channel turn, paid from the probe signer's escrow, whose signed\\\\nframes carry a `lookup` tool call with a JSON `query`. Each renewal keeps its\\\\ndeclared window length. Every other claimed feature has no probe yet and lapses.\\\\nWhatever is not renewed is left out of the file and lapses at its declared\\\\nexpiry. The command exits 1 when anything lapses and never prints the allowlist.\\\\nBefore each probe it requires one `--probe-escrow` free on the probe signer at the\\\\nfinalized head. When the signer holds less, no further probe runs, and stderr says\\\\n`gateway renew: PROBE SIGNER UNDERFUNDED: \u2026`.\\\\nThe GPU.ai single-instance response shape (`status`, `region`, `gpu_type`) is\\\\nassumed from the pricing and create APIs, so watch the first run.\\\\n\\\\nAn operator can instead publish an already settled owner-requested tools qualification\\\\nwithout creating another probe or using the direct renewer's signer/provider credentials:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop --network devnet gateway renew \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --catalog-env GATEWAY_MODEL_CATALOG --catalog-pricing chain \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --qualification-receipt ./settled-tools-qualification.json \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --qualification-receipt-sha256 \\\\\\\"$QUALIFICATION_RECEIPT_SHA256\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --out /opt/flop/gateway-evidence/gateway-evidence.json\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe hash must identify the exact immutable receipt bytes. Receipt-only mode rejects the\\\\ndirect-probe options. It verifies the original owner/resident/purpose envelope, signed\\\\nturn/prefix/ACK and canonical finalized positive settlement before appending one pass to\\\\nthe existing evidence file. It preserves unrelated deployments and conformance entries,\\\\nkeeps the proof-bound original probe time and existing declared window, and refuses a\\\\nconflicting re-publication. An identical receipt is a no-op. Concurrent `gateway renew`\\\\ncommands using this version take an exclusive publication lock; a conflicting writer\\\\nfails rather than replacing its contents. Older or unrelated writers must be coordinated\\\\nseparately. Receipt-only publication retains only this producer's latest unexpired pass\\\\nper exact model/feature identity, preserving its original times and all unrelated evidence.\\\\nA process killed while writing can leave `OUT.lock`; confirm that writer has stopped before\\\\nmanually recovering that lock, and never remove another active writer's lock.\\\\nNo fresh inference, escrow, signature submission or automatic publication by\\\\nthe qualification endpoint occurs. Ordinary chat continues to require fresh tools\\\\nadmission; a qualification request is not permission to run arbitrary stale-tools chat.\\\\n\\\\n#### Keys, hardware, multisig, and air-gapped signing\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nexport FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD='from-a-secret-manager'\\\\nflop keys generate --name treasury --out treasury.json \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD\\\\nexport FLOP_IMPORTED_SECRET='mnemonic from a secret manager'\\\\nflop keys import --secret-env FLOP_IMPORTED_SECRET --out imported.json \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD\\\\nflop keys export treasury.json --source-password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --out treasury-backup.json --password-env FLOP_BACKUP_PASSWORD\\\\nflop keys inspect treasury.json\\\\nflop keys hardware\\\\n\\\\nflop multisig address --threshold 2 --signatory <A> <B> <C>\\\\nflop --keystore treasury.json --password-env FLOP_KEY_PASSWORD \\\\\\\\\\\\n  multisig propose --threshold 2 --other <B> <C> --call <0x-call>\\\\nflop multisig list --account <MULTISIG>\\\\n\\\\nflop tx build --address <ADDRESS> --call <0x-call> \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --out unsigned.json --qr\\\\nflop tx broadcast unsigned.json --signature <0x-multisignature>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`tx build` pins genesis, runtime, transaction version, and nonce. Broadcast\\\\nrejects drift. Terminal QR uses optional `qrencode`; the JSON envelope works\\\\nwith Polkadot Vault, hardware wallets, HSM/MPC custody, or other detached\\\\nsigners.\\\\n\\\\n#### Wallets\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop wallet agent create <agent-address> --daily-cap 50 --tx-limit 5\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### Shared devnet agent credential\\\\nProvision one key for any supported agent client without launching Hermes:\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop --network devnet agent credential           # path, live model, quota; no bearer\\\\nflop --network devnet agent credential --json    # non-secret metadata\\\\nflop --network devnet agent credential --print-key # secret on stdout for local auth helpers\\\\nflop --network devnet agent credential --tailnet # private lane for approved Tailscale users\\\\n```\\\\nThe command requires explicit `--network devnet`. By default it enrolls at the\\\\npublic gateway `https://api.flop.network` with a wallet signature. On first use\\\\nit creates a local sr25519 account in `~/.flop/devnet-enroll-wallet.json`\\\\n(unencrypted, devnet only, mode 0600; its secret is never printed). If that\\\\naccount holds less than 1 FLOP, it requests a grant from\\\\n`https://faucet.flop.network/fund` and waits for the grant to finalize on\\\\n`wss://rpc.devnet.flop.network` (`--rpc` overrides). It then signs the\\\\ngateway's single-use challenge. The key is cached in\\\\n`~/.flop/devnet-wallet-agent-key.json`. The operator must explicitly fund and configure the allowance; the recommended\\\\ncasual-use grant is 20,000 devnet FLOP, scoped to the exact model returned by\\\\nenrollment, and expires within 24 hours. Re-enrolling\\\\nrotates the bearer but never renews quota or expiry.\\\\n\\\\n`--tailnet` keeps the private lane for approved Tailscale users. It enrolls at\\\\n`http://gateway.ts.flop.network:3201/enroll` and gives a seven-day allowance,\\\\ncached in `~/.flop/devnet-agent-key.json` and shared with the Hermes provider.\\\\nBoth caches are mode 0600 in a mode-0700 directory on POSIX systems. A `.lock`\\\\ndirectory per cache serializes enrollment across local clients. The\\\\n`--print-key` form is deliberately explicit; redirect or consume it privately\\\\nrather than recording terminal output. A stale `.lock` directory after a crash\\\\ncan be removed only after confirming no enrollment is running.\\\\n\\\\n`flop --network devnet agent init` and `agent doctor` use the public\\\\n`https://mcp.flop.network/mcp` read-only service by default; pass `--mcp-url`\\\\nto target another verified endpoint.\\\\n\\\\n#### Hermes Desktop\\\\nThe public native provider (`sdk/hermes_public`) is bundled with the\\\\nstandalone launcher 0.4.5. Use `flop hermes plugin install` in an isolated\\\\n`HERMES_HOME` after `hermes pm repair`, then `hermes auth add flop-public`, `hermes model` and\\\\n`hermes desktop`. The separate private provider (`sdk/hermes_native`)\\\\nrequires an approved Tailscale identity and FLOP repository access.\\\\nFollow the public native setup guide (`docs/integrations/hermes-public-launcher.md`,\\\\n\\\\\\\"Native public provider\\\\\\\") for the recommended public route. The full CLI also retains the private tailnet lane:\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop --network devnet hermes desktop --dry-run --json # inspect without provisioning\\\\nflop --network devnet hermes desktop --gateway http://gateway.ts.flop.network # tailnet lane\\\\n```\\\\nFrom a source checkout, replace `flop` with `node sdk/cli/dist/cli.js` after\\\\nthe build above.\\\\nThe alternate public hosted launcher requires managed-home preparation described\\\\nin the public guide; an immediate Desktop launch is not qualified. With the\\\\ntailnet `--gateway`, the devnet operator must approve your Tailscale user ID\\\\nfirst. The CLI then obtains a seven-day, 25 FLOP model-scoped allowance and\\\\nstores the key in `~/.flop/devnet-agent-key.json` (mode 0600). Later launches\\\\nand other local agent clients check and reuse the cached key.\\\\nIf the local key is lost or rejected, enrollment rotates the bearer while preserving\\\\nits spent amount and expiry. Exhausted, expired, and revoked allowances require an\\\\noperator to renew or reapprove them. Normal CLI output does not print the key.\\\\n\\\\nWithout `--network devnet`, the command starts the embedded signer proxy as before:\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop hermes desktop                                  # embedded proxy + launch Hermes\\\\nflop --signer //Bob hermes desktop                   # settle under //Bob\\\\nflop hermes desktop --model llama-3-8b-instruct --max-flop 10 --max-tokens 4096\\\\nflop hermes desktop --proxy-port 1234                # embedded proxy on a custom port\\\\nflop --network devnet --signer \\\\\\\"$FLOP_SIGNER\\\\\\\" hermes desktop --proxy # funded signer\\\\nflop hermes desktop --configure                      # also persist via `hermes config set`\\\\nflop hermes desktop --no-proxy \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --gateway http://gateway.ts.flop.network --model \\\\\\\"$FLOP_MODEL\\\\\\\"\\\\nflop hermes desktop --dry-run --json                 # print resolved env/launch plan, don't launch\\\\n```\\\\nIt wires Hermes to the embedded proxy via the env vars Hermes reads for a custom\\\\nOpenAI-compatible endpoint \u2014 `OPENAI_BASE_URL` (\u2192 proxy `/v1`), `OPENAI_API_KEY`,\\\\nand `HERMES_INFERENCE_MODEL` (`api_mode` auto-detects `chat_completions`) \u2014 plus\\\\n`FLOP_WS_URL`/`FLOP_SIGNER` for the `@flop-labs/hermes-plugin`. `--configure`\\\\nadditionally persists the wiring through the real `hermes config set` CLI\\\\n(`model.provider=custom`, `model.base_url`, `model.api_mode`, `model.default`).\\\\nRequires the Hermes binary (`hermes-desktop` or `hermes`) on `PATH`; use\\\\n`--dry-run` to inspect without it. A custom hosted `--gateway` requires\\\\n`FLOP_API_KEY` supplied privately and an explicit `--model` from the live\\\\ncatalog. The CLI checks gateway health, model availability, and key validity\\\\nbefore launching. The private devnet gateway is reachable only from the FLOP\\\\ntailnet.\\\\n\\\\n#### Local OpenAI Proxy\\\\nExpose a local OpenAI-compatible API (like LM Studio / Ollama's local server)\\\\nwhere **every request is submitted and settled on-chain under your signer**.\\\\nThe proxy estimates G_n, submits the PoUI task, waits for a TEE miner to settle\\\\nit, then returns the result \u2014 all behind the OpenAI REST schema:\\\\n```bash\\\\nflop proxy                                   # http://127.0.0.1:3201/v1\\\\nflop --signer //Bob proxy --max-flop 10\\\\nflop proxy --port 1234 --host 0.0.0.0        # expose beyond localhost\\\\n```\\\\n| Endpoint | Purpose |\\\\n|----------|---------|\\\\n| `POST /v1/chat/completions` | Chat inference (OpenAI-compatible), `stream: true` supported |\\\\n| `POST /v1/completions` | Text completion, `stream: true` supported |\\\\n| `GET /v1/models` | List models (live from the payload gateway, falls back to defaults) |\\\\n| `GET /v1/models/{id}` | Retrieve a single model |\\\\n| `POST /v1/embeddings` | Embeddings, computed **locally** (no chain) \u2014 see below |\\\\n| `GET /health` | Liveness |\\\\n| `OPTIONS *` | CORS preflight (permissive, for browser/Electron clients) |\\\\n\\\\n**Embeddings** are a cheap, high-frequency RAG primitive and don't need on-chain\\\\nsettlement, so the proxy computes them **locally** with a small embedding model\\\\n(default `Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, L2-normalized output like Ollama's\\\\n`/api/embed`). This needs the optional runtime dependency \u2014 install once:\\\\n```bash\\\\npnpm add @huggingface/transformers\\\\n```\\\\nWithout it, `/v1/embeddings` returns `501` with this hint (chat/completions are\\\\nunaffected). Override the model with `--embedding-model <hf-id>`.\\\\n\\\\n**Streaming:** `stream: true` returns OpenAI SSE chunks (`data: {\u2026}` \u2026 `data: [DONE]`),\\\\nincl. an optional usage chunk via `stream_options.include_usage`. FLOP settles a\\\\ntask atomically, so this is *settle-then-stream*: the result is awaited, then\\\\nemitted as chunks (latency-to-first-token = settlement time), not incremental\\\\nminer generation.\\\\n\\\\n**Models:** `/v1/models` reflects the payload gateway's registry\\\\n(`<payload-gateway>/v1/models`), falling back to the built-in defaults if it's\\\\nunreachable.\\\\n\\\\nOptions: `--port` (3201), `--host` (127.0.0.1), `--payload-gateway`\\\\n(off-chain prompt/result data plane, default `http://localhost:3200`),\\\\n`--model`, `--max-tokens` (default 2048), `--max-flop`. Uses global\\\\n`--rpc`/`--signer`. Point any OpenAI client at it via\\\\n`OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3201/v1`.\\\\n\\\\n## Architecture\\\\n\\\\n- Built with Commander.js\\\\n- Uses local SDK via `\\\\\\\"@flop-labs/sdk\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"file:../typescript\\\\\\\"`\\\\n- TypeScript with ES modules, compiled via `tsc`\\\\n- All commands use `FlopClient.create()` from the SDK with `--rpc` and `--signer` global options\\\\n- Role groups reuse existing launch, proxy, key, wallet, session, staking, TDX,\\\\n  and provider workflows rather than introducing parallel implementations.\\\\n\\\\nOperator images: use `ghcr.io/flop-labs/flop-core/cli:stable` (minimum 0.1.172),\\\\n`ghcr.io/flop-labs/flop-core/miner-worker:stable` (minimum 0.1.172), and\\\\n`ghcr.io/flop-labs/flop-core/miner-vllm-toploc:stable` (minimum 0.1.172).\\\\nFor a reproducible pin, use the version and digest in [releases.json](https://flop.network/releases.json).\\\\n`just miner-pack /tmp/flop-miner-pack` copies that manifest and fills the worker and backend image pins.\\\\n\\\",\\\"readmeFilename\\\":\\\"README.md\\\"}\",\"lastModified\":\"Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:13:08 GMT\"},{\"source\":\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@flop-labs/pi\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:32.209Z\",\"body\":\"{\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/pi\\\",\\\"_rev\\\":\\\"3-0d792f97db38d7ac88945d3b3d60934e\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/pi\\\",\\\"dist-tags\\\":{\\\"latest\\\":\\\"0.3.1\\\"},\\\"versions\\\":{\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/pi\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/pi@0.0.0-stage\\\",\\\"stub\\\":true,\\\"maintainers\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"}],\\\"dist\\\":{\\\"shasum\\\":\\\"4c5e411ca41ea79635bba6b8e6a404aa3a0